# Leaks the leak sentinel tolerates for now (docs/process.md, "The leak sentinel"); tools/check/sentinel.py checks
# the file, and the list only shrinks. <mode> | <target> | <kinds> | <reason>
#   allow      <target> (a test class, or Class.method) may leave the <kinds> (comma-separated; registry kinds such as
#              h3.serverRequest, or ksl.ssl, ksl.key, ksl.session, ksl.udp, ksl.wake) open; the reason says why (one
#              that a pending fix removes names its branch or commit)
#   per-class  <target> (a test class) is checked once after all its tests, not after each (fixtures shared across its
#              tests); <kinds> is `-`
allow | io.kuicksilver.ktor.client.contract.ContentTest.testBodyChannelCancelledWhenCallerScopeIsCancelled | tcp.socket | Ktor's vendored contract tests share one server; when the client cancels a download, the server's side of that connection ends with the handler's next write, after the test
allow | io.kuicksilver.ktor.client.contract.ContentTest.testDownloadStreamChannelWithCancel | tcp.socket | as the entry above: the shared server's side of the cancelled download ends with the handler's next write, after the test
allow | io.kuicksilver.ktor.client.contract.HttpTimeoutTest | tcp.socket | Ktor's vendored contract tests share one server whose timeout routes wait up to 10 s between writes; the server's side of a connection the client gave up on ends with the next write, after the test
